{title: 124 - Away in a Manger}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #124 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 124}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C7/Bb]Away [F/A]in [C7/Bb]amanger, [Dm]no [C]crib [Dm/A]for [Gm/D]abed,
[C]The little [Bb]Lord [C]Je [F/C]sus laid down [Gm/Bb]his sweet [F]head.
[C7/Bb]The [F]stars in [C7/Bb]the [Dm/A]bright sky [C7/Bb]looked down [C]where [Dm/A]he [Bb]lay,
[Am]The little [Gm/D]Lord [F/C]Je sus asleep [Gm]on [C/G]the hay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C7/Bb]The [F/C]cattle [C7/Bb]are lowing, [Dm]the baby [C]awakes,
[C]But little [Bb]Lord [C]Jesus [F]no crying [Gm/Bb]he makes.
[C7/Bb]I [F]love Thee, [C7/Bb]Lord [Dm/A]Jesus, [C7/Bb]look down [C]from [Dm/A]the [Bb]sky
[Am]And stay [Gm]by my [F/C]cradle til morning [C/G]is nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C7/Bb]Be [F/C]near me, [C7/Bb]Lord [Dm/A]Jesus, I ask [C]Thee [Dm/A]to [Gm/D]stay
[C]Close by [Bb]me forever, [F]and love [Gm/Bb]me, I [F]pray.
[C7/Bb]Bless [F]all the [C7/Bb]dear [Dm/A]children [C7/Bb]in thy [C]tender [Bb]care,
[Am]And take [Gm]us to [F/C]heaven, to live [Gm]with [C/G]Thee there.
{end_of_verse}
